    "Plan: Shadow 4 weeks — new model scores everything, decisions still made by champion; exit criteria: score correlation in expected band, disagreement cases (old approve/new decline and inverse) individually reviewed by credit officers, PSI between shadow and training population < 0.10. Canary: 10% of applications by random assignment (not by branch — selection bias), 2 weeks; rollback triggers pre-committed: approval-rate shift >1.5pp from forecast, AIR below 0.93, override rate >2× baseline. Sign-offs: platform (serving), Marcus (business), and the validation conditions checked as done by Model Risk. Then 100% with the first monthly monitoring report due 30 days later. Boring, staged, reversible — the way production changes should feel.",
