    "Fix order: (1) indirect injection via retrieved docs (high/medium — it's reachable by any employee's document), (2) prompt injection exfiltrating system prompt, (3) tool-call forgery on the agent (blocked by graph but the attempt path gets monitoring), then the rest. Promotions: direct injection suite and tool-forgery — both are one golden-set run from regressing silently with any model swap, which is exactly what regression tests are for. CISO brief: '8 findings this cycle, 5 closed, 0 critical open; injection resilience 94% and now release-gating; agent graph blocked all privilege attempts; next cycle: vector-store poisoning depth. Ask: none.' Five lines, upward-ready.",
